6. Core Nodes
🔧 6.1 motor_controller_node
Purpose:

Low-level motor control using Motor HAT.

Input:
/cmd_vel (geometry_msgs/Twist)
Output:
/motor_pwm (debug)
Logic:
left  = linear_x - k_turn * angular_z
right = linear_x + k_turn * angular_z

Scale to PWM:

pwm_left  = clamp(left * max_pwm)
pwm_right = clamp(right * max_pwm)
Requirements:
Parameters:
max_pwm
k_turn
deadzone
Must include:
class MotorDriver:
    def set_motor_speeds(left_pwm, right_pwm):
        pass

(Hardware abstraction required)

🧭 6.2 imu_stabilizer_node (CRITICAL)
Purpose:

Correct yaw drift without encoders.

Inputs:
/cmd_vel_in
/imu/data
Output:
/cmd_vel_out
Algorithm:
expected = cmd_vel.angular.z
measured = imu.angular_velocity.z

error = expected - measured

correction = Kp * error

adjusted_angular = cmd_vel.angular.z + correction
Requirements:
Parameter:
Kp
enabled (bool)
Must allow runtime tuning
